  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "",
    "overview": "This is a source-derived record of the website after the authorized homepage replacement on October 18, 2026. The shared visual base is a self-hosted sans serif, light neutral ground, graphite text, gold accents, rounded controls and ruled content. The Deviny name and existing logo are established assets. The homepage adds a campaign-scale typographic hierarchy and broad light, graphite and gold areas. Its composition is page-specific; the surface direction remains in `.impeccable/surfaces/scripts-build-py.md` and is not a new global brand requirement.\n\n`global.css` supplies the shared styles. The builder loads `home.css` and `home.js` only on the EN, RU and AZ homepages. Frontmatter names prefixed `home-` describe those overrides; unprefixed names describe the shared base. Other routes retain their shared layouts and components. Obsolete image-cover styles still present in `global.css` are not the current homepage and do not define this record.\n\n**Rendered QA is pending.** The prior localhost browser security denial remains in force, with no workaround used. There are no current desktop/mobile captures and no basis for claiming owner-approved branding or visual verification. `.impeccable/review/home-redesign-source-notes.json` records 58 detector findings: 49 old-design-system advisories and 9 warning instances. The warnings have not been declared clean; contrast, overflow, enlarged text and media-context findings still require rendered review. The finish verdict in `.impeccable/review/home-redesign-verdict.md` is `recapture`, requesting current full-page desktop (1440px) and mobile (390px) evidence before a new finish review. The source provenance scan covered 4 rasters with 0 missing records; provenance is not visual QA.\n\nOctober 20 ordinary extension: the repetitive five-topic feature index is superseded by a distributed semantic homepage story: people/GymBro, gold club emblem, program-format sheets, graphite communication, training/tools, staggered progression, privacy/choice and professional tools, then FAQ/stores. All 28 feature IDs occur once per EN/RU/AZ homepage. Global token metadata is preserved; these compositions belong to the surface brief. Program sheets stack up to 520px with auto height, 24px headings and 15px body text. The current independent source review disposition is recapture; no current page screenshots or desktop/mobile visual acceptance are available under the prior browser security denial. No new raster, font or dependency was introduced.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
